**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.PlannerInformationTests`

**How to implement.** The Measurement Planner's layer-2 core: the Fisher information of a set of candidate experiments, its rank, its confounded combinations and the Cramér–Rao bound per target (001 §M 'Layer 2, numerical (local, at a nominal point): the Fisher information from the Jacobians of every candidate experiment …; rank (identifiable combinations); smallest singular vectors (confounded combinations, e.g. thickness ↔ n); Cramér–Rao bounds per target'; the S14.2 brief). It REUSES `ResidualJacobian` (`MuellerInverse.fs:ResidualJacobian`: its `rank`, step 394, and `conditionNumber`), `FitQuality.covarianceOf` (step 476) and `FitUncertainty.ParameterWeights` (step 342); no second inverse, rank floor or condition number is written. The information of candidates whose rows J_i carry noise variances σ_i² is F = Σ J_iᵀ J_i / σ_i², and the bound per target is √diag(F⁻¹). The rows are kept scaled to one reference noise, the first candidate's, so the bound is `covarianceOf` of those rows with that noise as its reduced χ²: by construction the covariance a fit of those candidates reports when its residual level is their noise, which the promoted `predictedRelativeErrors` reads (step 342). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S14.2; every case name has two words; no `bool` appears. (1) Domain, `MeasurementPlanner.fs`, after step 472's members, because the planner's cache stores them (step 485): `NoiseVariance of float` with `.value`, the variance of one residual entry of a candidate in its residual's units squared; `CandidateRows = { jacobian : ResidualJacobian; noise : NoiseVariance }`, one candidate's information, its residual Jacobian over the targets' scaled coordinates and its entries' noise; and `PlannerError` (step 469) gains `NoiselessPlannerCandidateErr` (`the candidate's noise variance is not above zero: <reason>`) and `PlannerShapeErr` (`the candidate's Jacobian does not fit the targets: <reason>`), each `of reason : string` with its `describe` arm. (2) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/PlannerInformation.fs`, `module PlannerInformation` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Optimization`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj`'s compile list (one `<Compile Include="PlannerInformation.fs" />` line, no comment), because it reads `FitQuality`, `FitUncertainty`, `MuellerFitting`, `BenchNoise`, `FittedProblems` (step 476) and `StudyEngine`. Module doc: the Measurement Planner's numerical layer, the Fisher information of candidate experiments at a nominal point (spec 0050 S14.2). In order: (a) `SingularValue of float` with `.value`. (b) `[<Softellect.Sys.NumericCarrier("the singular values and right singular vectors of a residual Jacobian, read whole from the MathNet SVD")>] SingularSpectrum = { values : float[]; rightVectors : float[][] }`, with `static member ofRows (rows : float[][]) (coordinateCount : int) : SingularSpectrum`, marked `[<ElevationBoundary(nameof InteropBoundary, "the MathNet SVD of a residual Jacobian, its right singular vectors read whole")>]` (AGENTS.md: a call into a third-party numeric library is marked on its own declaration): with no row, `coordinateCount` zeros and the identity's rows; otherwise `Svd(true)` of `RealMatrix.create rows`, reached as `MuellerInverse.fs:conditionNumber` reaches it, its `S` in MathNet's descending order padded with zeros to `coordinateCount` and the rows of its `VT`. (c) `SingularDirection = { singularValue : SingularValue; weights : ParameterWeights }`, with `member this.text (coordinates : ParameterName list) : string`: each coordinate whose weight is at least a tenth of the largest in magnitude, in coordinate order, written `+<w> <name>` or `-<w> <name>` with two decimals under `CultureInfo.InvariantCulture`, joined by single spaces. (d) `InformationLogDeterminant of float` and `CovarianceTrace of float`, each with `.value`. (e) `TargetBound = { name : ParameterName; sigma : ParameterSigma }` (`ParameterSigma`, S7.1 step 214). (f) `PlannerInformation = { coordinates : ParameterName list; rows : ResidualJacobian; noise : NoiseVariance }`: the targets, every candidate's rows stacked in order, each multiplied by √(noise / its noise), and the reference noise, the first candidate's (`NoiseVariance 1.0` with none). `static member over (coordinates : ParameterName list) (candidates : CandidateRows list) : Result<PlannerInformation, PlannerError>`: a candidate whose noise is not finite or not above zero answers `NoiselessPlannerCandidateErr` naming its 1-based position and noise, and one whose rows do not each hold one entry per coordinate `PlannerShapeErr` naming its position and both counts; nothing is answered in part. Members: `this.rank : MatrixRank`, `this.rows.rank` (`MatrixRank 0` with no row, step 394); `this.spectrum : SingularSpectrum`, `SingularSpectrum.ofRows` of the rows and the coordinate count; `this.confounded : SingularDirection list`, the spectrum's directions from index `rank` on, in its order: the combinations the candidates do not determine, below step 394's floor; `this.weakestOpt : SingularDirection option`, the direction at index `rank − 1` when the rank is at least one, the identifiable combination determined worst; `this.conditionOpt : ConditionNumber option`, `this.rows.conditionNumber` (`MuellerInverse.fs:conditionNumber`) when the rank equals the coordinate count and it is finite; `this.scaledSigmasOpt : DesignVector option`, at full rank the square roots of the diagonal of `FitQuality.covarianceOf this.rows (ReducedChiSquared this.noise.value)` in coordinate order, the Cramér–Rao bound in the scaled coordinates, and `None` otherwise; `this.logDeterminant : InformationLogDeterminant`, the sum over the first `rank` singular values s of 2 · ln s, less `rank · ln noise`, the log pseudo-determinant of F over its identifiable combinations (0 at rank 0); `this.traceOpt : CovarianceTrace option`, the sum of the squares of `scaledSigmasOpt` when it is `Some`; and `this.boundsOver (scaling : ParameterScaling<'Parameters>) : TargetBound list option` (`MuellerInverse.fs:ParameterScaling`), for `scaledSigmasOpt = Some s` each coordinate k's bound `ParameterSigma (s_k · |axis.read scaling.scale|)`, the axis being `scaling.axes`' k-th, the one the rows' coordinate k is scaled by, and `None` otherwise. (g) `type ReducedChiSquared with member this.noiseVariance : NoiseVariance` (`FitQuality.fs:ReducedChiSquared`): the noise variance a fit's reduced χ² estimates, the residual level of measured data read as a candidate's noise. No cache, threshold, regularisation or option is added. Tests: new `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PlannerInformationTests.fs`, `module PlannerInformationTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, over Jacobians written as literals and test-local coordinate names. `the Cramer-Rao bound is the covariance a fit reports when its residual level is the noise`: over the coordinates of `UniaxialParameters.axes`' first two axes (n_o, n_e), the candidate J = [[1; 0]; [1; 1]; [0; 2]] with noise 0.04 has `scaledSigmasOpt` [0.2 · √(5/9); 0.2 · √(2/9)] within 1e-12 ((JᵀJ)⁻¹ = [[5; −1]; [−1; 2]] / 9, written out in the test); the same rows as two candidates, the first row at noise 0.04 and the last two doubled at noise 0.16, give the same sigmas within 1e-12; and `boundsOver` a scaling over those two axes whose scale holds 1e-3 for both indices answers those sigmas times 1e-3 under the names n_o and n_e. `two coordinates the candidates move only together are one confounded combination`: over coordinates a, b and c, J = [[1; 1; 0]; [2; 2; 1]] at noise 1 has rank 2, `conditionOpt`, `scaledSigmasOpt` and `boundsOver` `None`, one confounded direction whose weights are ±(1/√2, −1/√2, 0) within 1e-12 and whose text is `+0.71 a -0.71 b` or `-0.71 a +0.71 b`, and a weakest direction whose singular value is above zero. `with no candidate nothing is identifiable, and a noiseless or misshapen candidate is refused`: over no candidate the rank is 0, the three confounded directions are the identity's and `logDeterminant` is 0; a candidate at noise 0 answers `NoiselessPlannerCandidateErr` naming candidate 1, and one of two columns over three coordinates `PlannerShapeErr` naming both counts, each `describe` starting with its rendered prefix. `the log determinant counts each identifiable combination, and the trace sums the targets' variances`: J = [[2; 0]; [0; 3]] at noise 1 has `logDeterminant` 2 ln 2 + 2 ln 3 and `traceOpt` 1/4 + 1/9, and at noise 4 `logDeterminant` 2 ln 2 + 2 ln 3 − 2 ln 4, each within 1e-12; and `(ReducedChiSquared 0.25).noiseVariance` is `NoiseVariance 0.25`.

**Acceptance.** After the core lands, `PlannerInformation.over` MUST stack each candidate's rows scaled to the reference noise and answer its rank, confounded and weakest combinations, condition, log determinant, trace and Cramér–Rao sigmas as `FitQuality.covarianceOf` gives them, refusing a noiseless or misshapen candidate; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the Cramer-Rao bound is the covariance a fit reports when its residual level is the noise`, `two coordinates the candidates move only together are one confounded combination`, `with no candidate nothing is identifiable, and a noiseless or misshapen candidate is refused` and `the log determinant counts each identifiable combination, and the trace sums the targets' variances`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s46 invariants MUST pass.
